+// --- XStreaming patch: direct native (non-JSI) access to the default MMKV
+// instance's "user.settings" key, for a Kotlin-only settings UI that doesn't
+// go through the JS bridge at all. MMKV::mmkvWithID(...) (used further
+// below) returns the SAME process-wide singleton instance JS's `new MMKV()`
+// (id "mmkv.default", no explicit path) already uses. Calling this from a
+// SEPARATE MMKV dependency/instance would NOT be safe (two independent
+// copies of MMKV's C++ core racing the same mmap'd file); this works only
+// because it's compiled into this exact same reactnativemmkv.so, sharing
+// MMKV's one static instance registry with nativeInstall below.
+//
+// mmkvRootDirReady() checks MMKV::getRootDir() rather than just assuming
+// nativeInstall has already run initializeMMKV(): that's normally true well
+// before any native UI reachable only from within the already-running app
+// could call this (shared/lib/mmkv.ts's `new MMKV()` runs at JS module-
+// import time), EXCEPT when Android recreates a native-only Activity
+// directly after the whole process was killed in the background -- that
+// Activity can then become the very first code to run in the new process,
+// with RN/JS never having started at all. nativeEnsureMmkvInitialized below
+// covers that case explicitly, with the guarantee that whichever of it and
+// nativeInstall actually runs initializeMMKV() first, the other's call is a
+// no-op against the identical root directory (see both functions' bodies)
+// -- defined up here, before nativeInstall, so nativeInstall's own guard
+// below can call it.
+bool mmkvRootDirReady() {
+  return !MMKV::getRootDir().empty();
+}
